# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        name: "Buggie"
        url: "https://buggie.eu"
      }
      description: `Buggie is bug tracking that starts with a good report: a tracker for people who
build things for clients, whose reporter widget captures the screenshot, the
console and the failing request at the moment something broke. It is AGPL-3.0 and
self-hostable, with a hosted service at buggie.eu.

This definition covers both HTTP APIs Buggie documents for its users:

- **The token API** (\`/v1\`), for scripting against a workspace: listing, reading,
filing and updating issues, and listing projects. It lives on the workspace's own
subdomain and is authenticated by a personal access token made under
Settings → Workspace → API tokens, with the abilities \`read\` and/or \`write\`.
Tokens are for members of staff: a client's token is refused with 403.
Requests are limited to 120 a minute per token.
- **The reporter ingest API** (\`/ingest\`), which the web widget and the native
SDKs post bug reports to. It is unauthenticated and keyed by a project's public
widget key. It is documented on the central domain, \`https://buggie.eu/api\`, or
a self-hosted install's own domain.

Not covered, deliberately: the inbound-mail webhook (\`/mail/inbound\`), which is a
Mailgun callback rather than an API for Buggie's users; the webhooks Buggie sends
to you (https://buggie.eu/docs/webhooks); and the application's own screens.

Unofficial definition authored by Voxgig from Buggie's public source
(https://github.com/bpowerie25/buggie: \`routes/api.php\`, the \`Api\` controllers and
the form requests they validate with) and its documentation
(https://buggie.eu/docs/api, https://buggie.eu/docs/native-sdks), and verified
against a self-hosted instance built from that source. Not an official Buggie
document.
`
      security: {
        in: "header"
        name: "Authorization"
        prefix: "Bearer"
        scheme: "bearerAuth"
        type: "http"
      }
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Buggie (hosted). The token API answers on the workspace's own subdomain. A self-hosted install serves the same paths on its own domain."
          url: "https://{workspace}.buggie.eu/api"
          variables: {
            workspace: {
              default: "your-workspace"
              description: "The workspace's subdomain, e.g. `acme` for `acme.buggie.eu`. A token works only in the workspace it was made in; anywhere else it gets 404."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
      summary: "Buggie is bug tracking that starts with a good report: a tracker for people who build things for clients, whose reporter widget captures the screenshot, the console and the failing request at the moment something broke."
      title: "Buggie API"
      version: "1.0.0"
      website: "https://buggie.eu/docs/api"
    }
  }
}

